rachel_cs: Heads-up: MedMetric onboarding blocked on staging. Browser SDK clients intermittently hit 401s during token exchange, then we see bursts of 429s from their QA harness. Started ~11:12 UTC. Can someone help triage?

julie_prod: I grabbed their staging logs. Pattern: lots of short-lived browser tabs doing ephemeral preflight + immediate API calls. Log excerpt: 
```
[2026-03-22T11:12:08Z] auth: POST /token -> 200 {token: xxx} 
[2026-03-22T11:12:08Z] client: POST /v1/chat -> 401 {"err":"nbf: token not active"}
[2026-03-22T11:12:09Z] auth: POST /token -> 200 {token: yyy}
[2026-03-22T11:12:09Z] client: POST /v1/chat -> 429 {"err":"rate_limit.exceeded"}
```
They say tokens are minted by their auth server on the same AWS region.

tom_eng: Two likely causes: 1) token nbf set slightly in future (SSO or clock skew), 2) their test harness opens hundreds of parallel sessions so once tokens become valid they all hit at once. Quick repro: we saw a 400ms cluster of requests after ~1s where 80% fail with 429.

jeff_infra: Can you ask them to decode the JWT and share iat/nbf/exp? Also which clock source on their QA machines? Docker images historically shipped without NTP in that org.

julie_prod: Decoded JWTs show nbf = 1711143120, iat = 1711143120. Our server time is ~3s ahead of their QA runners.

rachel_cs: So their machines are behind (client time older) meaning token says "not before" that client time sees as in the future and rejects?

tom_eng: Exactly. The browser or SDK tries using token immediately and backend rejects until client time reaches nbf window. Then many tabs retry in tight loop -> sudden burst -> 429.

jeff_infra: Short-term: we can suggest client-side: accept small clock skew when validating (browser libs usually fine) but main fix is to avoid simultaneous refreshes. Recommend single-token-per-origin pattern and short in-memory cache with jittered refresh.

julie_prod: Suggested quick SDK snippet for browser: 
```
let tokenPromise = null;
async function getEphemeralToken() {
  if (tokenPromise) return tokenPromise;
  tokenPromise = (async () => {
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Math.random() * 200)); // jitter
    const t = await fetch('/session-token');
    setTimeout(() => { tokenPromise = null; }, 1000); // cache for 1s
    return t.json();
  })();
  return tokenPromise;
}
```
Then use exponential backoff with capped retries on 401 -> treat 401 as possible nbf and retry once after small delay rather than immediate fanout.

tom_eng: Server-side: we can add a small 5-10s acceptance window for nbf offsets <= 5s to reduce false 401s from tight clocks. Also we should detect identical client fingerprints sending many token refreshes and count as one for rate-limiter (merge by origin+user-agent). Can do quick config change for their account.

rachel_cs: Billing note: medmetric will likely request leniency during onboarding. Can we do a temporary burst allowance?

rate-bot: AUTO: Support ticket PD-47210 created and assigned to rachel_cs, priority: high.

jeff_infra: I can patch their account to allow a 60s burst window for 24 hours if billing approves. Recommend we ask ops to confirm their QA images have NTP.

julie_prod: Customer ops confirmed they'll enable systemd-timesyncd on their runner images within the hour and will apply SDK change to QA harness.

tom_eng: I'll prepare a small DevEx note: "Browser ephemeral tokens + parallel tabs -> 401 then 429. Fix: single-token pattern, jitter, cached promise, verify NTP." Add sample code above and a short diag checklist.

rachel_cs: Action items: 1) MedMetric: enable NTP on runners (owner: medmetric ops) 2) MedMetric: deploy SDK single-token caching + jitter (owner: medmetric dev lead) 3) Redwood: enable 24h burst window (owner: jeff_infra, pending billing) 4) Redwood Eng: small nbf tolerance + dedupe refresh in rate-limiter (owner: tom_eng). ETA: updates by EOD.

jeff_infra: Billing approved 24h burst for onboarding. I've applied it.

julie_prod: After applying SDK patch in QA (300 parallel tabs), no 401s and no 429 cascade on 15m soak. Customer confirmed staging ready to proceed.

rate-bot: AUTO: PD-47210 closed by rachel_cs

rachel_cs: Closing thread  medmetric onboarding unblocked. Will follow up with DevEx doc update tomorrow. Thanks all!
